### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a rectangular block with some content) that flips/rotates when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & container ---------- */
body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card wrapper (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself ---------- */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth rotation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front side ---------- */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front styling */
.card .front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    color:#333;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* Back styling */
.card .back {
    background:#4caf50;
    color:#fff;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* start flipped */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    font-size:1.2rem;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);       /* flip on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over this card to see the back.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Thanks for hovering!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives the 3D effect; without it the rotation would look flat. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements (`front`, `back`) in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back side | Positions the back side initially flipped so that it becomes visible when the card rotates. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the whole card on mouseover. |

#### Customization tips

- Change `rotateY` to `rotateX` if you want a vertical flip instead of horizontal.
- Adjust `perspective` value for more or less depth.
- Add more content or images inside `.front` / `.back`.
- Use `transition: transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(...)` for different easing.

Enjoy your rotating card!
